# pyenv
#   For a library or package, you might want to ignore these files. For applications,
#   if you want to commit those files, uncomment the following lines
# .python-version

# pipenv
#   According to pypa/pipenv#598, it is recommended to include Pipfile.lock in version
#   control. However, in case of collaboration, if having platform-specific dependencies
#   or dependencies not having cross-platform support, pipenv may install dependencies
#   that do not work on all platforms.
# Pipfile.lock

# UV
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include uv.lock in version
#   control. This ensures that the installed package versions are fully reproducible.
# uv.lock

# poetry
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include poetry.lock in version
#   control. This is especially recommended for binary packages to ensure reproducibility.
#   https://python-poetry.org/basic-usage/#commit-your-lockfile-to-version-control
# poetry.lock
# poetry.toml

# pdm
#   Similar to Pipfile.lock, it is generally recommended to include pdm.lock in version
#   control.
# pdm.lock
# pdm.toml

# PEP 582; used by e.g. github.com/David-OConnor/pyflow and github.com/David-OConnor/pdm-project
__pypackages__/

